        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string>Clone (duplicate) an existing ERP5 document.\n
\n
    Creates a copy of the document with all its fields and sub-objects. Much faster\n
    than creating from scratch when you have a well-configured template document.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need a new document similar to an existing one (e.g. clone a Sale Order).\n
    - Creating from scratch would require too many field edits.\n
    - The user says "copy", "duplicate", or "clone" an existing document.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You want to create a blank document — use erp5_create instead.\n
    - You want to edit an existing document — use erp5_write instead.\n
\n
    PREREQUISITE: Call erp5_read first to verify the document exists and has a\n
    \'clone_document\' action available in its workflow actions or views.\n
    </string> </value>
